{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST parse Rust, Python, TypeScript, CSS, Markdown, TOML, and YAML\nsources with pinned tree-sitter grammars, selected by file extension compared\ncase-insensitively. A source with any syntax error MUST fail to parse, reporting\nthe line of its first error. Every\nother text file MUST use a plain-text profile in which each line that is not\nblank is an anonymous outline node of kind `line`. Each supported language MUST\nhave an outline profile that maps grammar node kinds to short outline kind names\nand, for each mapped kind, states whether a node is named, and by which fields\nor children, or anonymous. Only mapped kinds MUST appear in the outline; other\nnodes MUST be transparent, so their outline descendants appear under the\nnearest outline ancestor. A profile MAY attach grammar siblings to an outline\nnode, such as Rust attributes and doc comments preceding an item, so the outline\ntree need not match the grammar tree exactly; attached siblings are part of that\nnode for its line range and hash. Every file's outline MUST have a root node\nfor the whole file, independent of language. Source in no other outline node,\nsuch as top-level statements no profile maps, MUST belong to the root node;\nprofiles MUST NOT invent fallback kinds for it. Comments MUST NOT be outline nodes. Profiles MUST be\ndocumented. Upgrading a grammar or profile MAY change outlines and MUST be\ntreated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. Each obligation in `requirements.references.outlines` maps to marked code and a test that asserts its outcome.\n\n**Pinned grammars, supported languages, case-insensitive extension selection**\n- `Cargo.toml` pins every tree-sitter crate exactly (`=0.27.1`, `=0.25.0`, and so on). That is configuration, not code.\n- `profiles()` and `profile_for_path` in `src/outline/profile.rs` select a profile by lowercased extension. Each language has its own `PROFILE` static: `rust.rs`, `python.rs`, `typescript.rs` (including `TSX_PROFILE`), `css.rs`, `markdown.rs`, `toml.rs` and `yaml.rs`.\n- `profiles_are_selected_by_extension_case_insensitively` tests this, including `LIB.RS`, `a.Py`, `a.TSX` and `README.MD`.\n\n**A syntax error fails the parse, with the line of the first error**\n- `parse_redacted` calls `check_errors` in `src/outline/mod.rs`. It walks to the first `ERROR` or `MISSING` node and returns `OutlineError { line }`.\n- `reports_parse_failures_with_lines` asserts the line for Rust, a late error in TOML (line 3), and a Python failure, and checks the `line N:` message format.\n- `OutlineCache::parse` in `src/inputs.rs` surfaces the failure as a `cannot parse … source` error.\n\n**Plain-text profile for every other text file**\n- `plain_text` makes one anonymous `line` node per non-blank line.\n- `plain_text_lines_are_interchangeable_anonymous_nodes` tests it. The `outline` tool test in `src/authoring/tools.rs` also checks `line` nodes, `null` names and blank-line skipping.\n\n**Profile mapping kinds to short names and naming rules**\n- `KindRule`, `NameRule` (`Anonymous`, `Field`, `FirstChild`, `Custom`) and the per-language `KINDS` tables carry this.\n- Per-language tests assert the resulting names:\n  - Python: `python_profile_outlines_defs_classes_and_statements`\n  - TypeScript: `typescript_profile_outlines_declarations`\n  - CSS: `css_profile_names_rules_by_normalized_selectors`\n  - Markdown: `markdown_profile_nests_sections_by_heading`\n  - TOML and YAML: `toml_and_yaml_profiles_name_keys`\n  - Rust: `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` and the `Outline`/`OutlineNode` tests\n\n**Only mapped kinds appear; other nodes are transparent**\n- `Builder::walk` recurses with the same parent for unmapped nodes.\n- The Python, TypeScript and CSS tests show unmapped statements and `@import` producing no nodes.\n\n**Attached siblings count toward the line range and hash**\n- The Rust and Python `attaches` functions, together with `walk` and `finish`, implement this.\n- The Python test expects `def[f] 2-5`, which includes the decorator and the leading comment.\n\n**Root node for the whole file, covering unmapped source, with no fallback kinds**\n- `root_node` is always node 0.\n- `file_level_inner_doc_comments_and_unmapped_code_belong_to_the_root` and `no_profile_invents_fallback_kinds` test these cases.\n\n**Comments are never outline nodes**\n- `Builder::maps` excludes comments, and comments are recorded separately.\n- The CSS, Markdown and Python tests show no comment nodes in the outline.\n\n**Profiles documented**\n- `md/reference.md`, section \"Outline profiles\", has a table of every profile with kinds, grammar nodes and naming. It also has per-language details and a statement that grammars are pinned exactly.\n- The table matches the code, including the `extern` ABI name, the item-position macro, and Markdown sections being anonymous before the first heading.\n\n**Upgrades are a deliberate change**\n- `md/reference.md` states that upgrading a grammar or changing a profile is a deliberate change. This is a process obligation, and the documentation carries it.\n\n**Marking and unspecified behavior**\n- The code that makes these decisions carries `{impl}` references to the requirement.\n- The tests carry `{test}` references.\n- The extra profile options (`trailing_comments_outside`, `when` conditions, `attaches`) are documented in the profile details, so they are not unspecified behavior.",
  "references": "da09d6fb6950407958a8419ece980b86c9589084282e9bceb13f58d875ee68ed",
